body:
Extends #119 / #115 with an executable compression ladder over the actual current renderers.

## Question

How much compression do we get before and after we begin dropping semantics?

## Same canonical report, four projections

The integration fixture builds one representative `AnalysisReport` with:

- report-level coordinate/support evidence;
- one explicit-coordination finding;
- finding-level supporting provenance receipts;
- one material `UNKNOWN`;
- one review/coordination question.

It then renders the exact same object as:

```text
human text
minified JSON
C1 lossless compact grammar
terse lossy projection
```

## Assertions

- C1 decodes byte-for-semantic-object back to the original report;
- C1 is smaller than minified JSON on the representative object;
- terse is smaller than both C1 and human text;
- terse retains the material UNKNOWN and question;
- terse omits support/provenance receipt strings that remain present in C1;
- the test explicitly refuses to treat terse as a round-trip storage format.

This makes the boundary executable:

```text
JSON -> C1
  compression without semantic loss

C1 -> terse
  additional compression by deliberate selection/omission
```

The second transition therefore needs the #125-style decision-preservation tests; byte savings alone are not evidence of correctness.

## Boundary

- research-only integration fixture;
- no renderer or schema changes;
- no claim that the representative report is a universal size distribution;
- no public CLI change;
- no claim that omitted provenance is unimportant, only that it remains recoverable from the canonical/lossless object.

Refs #67 #106 #109 #113 #115 #119 #121 #125.

## Summary

This PR durably migrates the Owner-approved Physical Products clean-sheet design control model under the existing authority of PB-DEC-501.

- records PB-DEC-502 for Clean-Sheet Physical Design Pipeline v0.1;
- adds the detailed durable pipeline operating document;
- records Bambu Lab P1S + AMS as current fabrication capability, with multicolor supported but optional;
- establishes physical-design gates G0–G6;
- records the `CLEAN_SHEET` geometry baseline;
- records `recovered_authoritative_geometry_files: 0`, meaning no recovered geometry artifact may serve as current PeptiBloom design authority; this does not erase historical concepts, renders, reported geometry or recovered legacy knowledge;
- keeps Bloom Caps at `PRE_G0`, with CAD unauthorized and common core `HYPOTHESIS_ONLY`;
- leaves PB-DEC-501 domain boundaries unchanged;
- does not grant `READY_FOR_SALE` or publication, Commerce, Legal/IP, procurement or payment authority;
- keeps `PB-XD REQUIRED NOW: NO`; no cross-domain contract is created;
- contains no private WORK 7 supplier, procurement, cost, logistics or other restricted operational data;
- does not approve storage implementation or assign permanent Physical Product/Design/Revision/Build/Validation IDs.

## Exact file scope

Exactly six files are changed:

1. `project/PHYSICAL_DESIGN_PIPELINE.md` — new
2. `project/DECISIONS.md`
3. `project/CANON.md`
4. `project/PROJECT_STATE.yaml`
5. `project/STATUS.md`
6. `project/HANDOFFS/physical-products.md`

No CAD, fabrication artifact, Git LFS configuration, external storage configuration, Web, Commerce, Operative Core, WORK 7/private-repository or BLOCKERS changes are included.

The held Bloom Caps Owner Input & Measurement Pack remains `DRAFT_PREPARED / HOLD` and is not promoted by this PR.
